        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e434bb41-b480-5ee3-ba4f-f6896bdf4681",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: FLEXcon\n- Products: Pressure-sensitive film products, barcodes, 2D codes\n- Applications: Advertising, product identification, safety and hazard labels, bar coded labels, primary labels, bonding and mounting\n- Systems: Barcode readers, smartphones with cameras, image-reading application software\n- Concepts: Geometric barcode patterns\n\nFacts:\n- FLEXcon is a worldwide manufacturer of pressure-sensitive film products.\n- FLEXcon's pressure-sensitive film products are used for indoor and outdoor advertising, product identification, safety and hazard labels, bar coded labels, primary labels, and bonding and mounting.\n- Later, two-dimensional codes were developed as a type of barcode.\n- Two-dimensional barcode codes used rectangles, dots, hexagons, and other geometric patterns in two dimensions rather than bars.\n- Barcodes were initially scanned by special optical scanners called barcode readers.\n- Later, application software enabled devices that could read images, such as smartphones with cameras, to scan barcodes.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1f7e1c94-61ea-5769-982e-6d0eda5a773e",
        "text": "Page: FLEXcon. Sentence: FLEXcon is a worldwide manufacturer of pressure-sensitive film products for applications that include indoor and outdoor advertising, product identification and safety/hazard labels, bar coded labels, primary labels and bonding/mounting.\nPage: Barcode. Sentence: Later two-dimensional (2D) codes were developed, using rectangles, dots, hexagons and other geometric patterns in two dimensions, usually called barcodes although they do not use bars as such.\nPage: Barcode. Sentence: Barcodes were initially scanned by special optical scanners called barcode readers. Later application software became available for devices that could read images, such as smartphones with cameras.",
